t b\", \"a   b\", \"a    b\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"empty_quotes_do_not_break_runs\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Removed empty quote delimiters create no emitted character or protected boundary; adjacent ordinary runs collapse together and outer runs trim.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A \\t\\\"\\\"\\r\\n B, \\\"\\\" \\tC\\\"\\\"\\r \",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a b\", \"c\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"normalization_before_deduplication\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Case folding, whitespace normalization, quote concatenation, and ordinary-character escaping all precede exact deduplication.\",\n+      \"input\": \" BETA ,A  B,\\\"a b\\\",a\\tB,be\\\"TA\\\",\\\\BETA,ALPHA,alpha\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"beta\", \"a b\", \"alpha\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"protected_equality_and_distinctions\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Deduplication compares final characters rather than protection metadata, while distinct protected whitespace multiplicities and characters remain distinct.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A B,\\\"A B\\\",A\\\\ B,\\\"A  B\\\",\\\"A\\tB\\\",A\\tB,\\\" \\\",\\\\ ,\\\"  \\\",\\\"\\t\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a b\", \"a  b\", \"a\\tb\", \" \", \"  \", \"\\t\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"literal_ascii_and_escape_next_only\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Preserve non-delimiter ASCII punctuation and controls; escaping letters removes only the backslash, never interprets escape names, and escaped uppercase lowercases in both modes.\",\n+      \"input\": \"\\\\N\\\\T\\\\R,\\\"\\\\A\\\\Z\\\",!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{};:'/?<>.|`~0129,\\u0000\\u001b\\u007f\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"ntr\", \"az\", \"!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{};:'/?<>.|`~0129\", \"\\u0000\\u001b\\u007f\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"paired_backslash_before_delimiter\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An escaped backslash consumes exactly its partner; a following comma still separates and a following quote still toggles mode.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A\\\\\\\\,B,C\\\\\\\\\\\"D,E\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a\\\\\", \"b\", \"c\\\\d,e\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_quote_and_later_toggle\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Escaped quotes concatenate as literal characters with later genuine quoted segments; separators inside the genuine segment remain literal.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A\\\\\\\"\\\"B,C\\\"D,\\\"E\\\\\\\"F\\\"G\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a\\\"b,cd\", \"e\\\"fg\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A trailing unpaired backslash invalidates the whole input despite previously valid and duplicate labels.\",\n+      \"input\": \"GOOD,good,OK,TAIL\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"unclosed_quote_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A quote opened in the middle of a later label must close; valid earlier labels and quoted commas cannot hide the whole-input error.\",\n+      \"input\": \"GOOD,OK,PRE\\\"TAIL,STILL\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_in_quote\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A trailing unpaired backslash also raises in quoted mode after otherwise valid labels.\",\n+      \"input\": \"GOOD,\\\"TAIL\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_final_quote_does_not_close\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An escaped final quote is literal and leaves quoted mode unclosed, invalidating previously valid labels too.\",\n+      \"input\": \"GOOD,\\\"TAIL\\\\\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"properties\": [\"unique_nonempty_labels\", \"ascii_lowercase\"],\n+  \"rationale\": \"The 22 deterministic ASCII cases cover every rule and their interactions. Empty and repeated-separator cases check discarding and order. Quote concatenation and literal delimiter cases exercise mode transitions anywhere in a label and escaping in both modes. All six ASCII whitespace characters are checked as ordinary, quoted, and escaped characters, with protected boundaries, protected-only labels, independent ordinary runs around protected characters, and empty quotes within runs. Lowercasing includes quoted and escaped uppercase. Deduplication is checked after normalization, across different protection histories, and against distinct protected whitespace. Literal punctuation and non-whitespace ASCII controls check exact preservation. Paired backslashes check consumption of exactly one next character. Four invalid suffix cases require whole-input ValueError after valid labels. Expectations follow boundary trimming before internal ordinary-run collapse, exact preservation of protected characters, ASCII lowercasing, empty removal, and stable exact deduplication.\"\n+}\n",
